  "term": "Leber’s disease",
  "definition": "Leber’s disease is a maternally inherited genetic disorder in which central vision is lost suddenly or over a short period, typically in mid-life, often progressing to a central blind spot and blindness. It is linked to missense mutations in mitochondrial DNA affecting polypeptides in respiratory chain complexes I, III, and IV.",
